{{Quote|Why didn't I think of it before? We're fighting a [[Failsafe|giant plant]] and I've got an alien that can control plants!|Ben before transforming into Swampfire.<ref name="IAEF">''[[If All Else Fails]]''</ref>}}
Swampfire has a high degree of chlorokinesis,{{Refn|[[:File:Swampfire's Chlorokinesis.PNG]]|group = DJW}} being able to telepathically interface with plant life and manipulate their growth.{{Refn|[https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ben10/images/3/38/AF_Mini_Bible.pdf  Alien Force Series Mini Bible]|group = AF Mini Bible|name = bible 4}} Some plants have a brief green aura when he influences them.<ref name="GT">''[[Ghost Town]]''</ref> After "blossoming", he was able to easily grow plants from the ground by simply raising his hand.<ref name="CIS" />

Aside from [[Earth (Classic)|Earth]] plants, Swampfire can use his telepathic plant interface with alien plant life, which was what allowed him to free [[Max Tennyson (Classic)|Max]] from the [[Failsafe]].<ref name="IAEF" /> He could also control the plants on [[Vilgaxia]].<ref name="GT" /> In his "blossomed" form, his telepathic influence over plants has extended to sentient plant life, such as the [[Magical Pumpkin]] from [[Anur Transyl]].<ref name="CIS" />

Swampfire's body produces large amounts of highly flammable methane gas, which he has the ability to ignite in his palms similar to a flamethrower.{{Refn|group = AF Mini Bible|name = bible 4}} This allows him to spew out a steady stream of fire that can melt steel<ref name="XB2">''[[X = Ben + 2]]''</ref> and blow up a train car.<ref name="B10RP1" /> He can create fireballs that allow him to disperse a large group of enemies<ref name="ETAtW" /> and harm more powerful beings like [[Vaxasaurian (Classic)|Vaxasaurians]],<ref name="GCBC">''[[Good Copy, Bad Copy]]''</ref> [[Highbreed]],<ref name="WotW2">''[[War of the Worlds: Part 2]]''</ref> and [[Tetramand (Classic)|Tetramands]].<ref>''[[Plumbers' Helpers (Episode)|Plumbers' Helpers]]''</ref> Swampfire can also expel fire from his mouth, as demonstrated by [[Swamps]].<ref name="DoN">''[[Double or Nothing]]''</ref> 

Swampfire's methane has a very pungent smell that is intolerable to some species like the [[Incursean (Classic)|Incurseans]], which will make them retch and faint.<ref name="XB2" /> By spraying methane point-blank, he can render [[Human (Classic)|humans]] unconscious.<ref>''[[The Final Battle: Part 1]]''</ref>

Swampfire is capable of limited flight through means of launching fire from his palms as jet propulsion, much like [[Heatblast (Classic)|Heatblast]].<ref>''[[War of the Worlds: Part 1]]''</ref>

Swampfire can generate seeds from his body that phase into or pierce into any ground or flooring before turning to vine tentacles strong enough to restrain a [[Highbreed]]<ref name="WotW2" /> and a [[Chimera Sui Generis (Classic)|Chimera Sui Generis]].<ref name="TFBP2">''[[The Final Battle: Part 2]]''</ref> He can also spawn similar structures on his body in a form of vine tentacles.<ref>''[[Fame]]''</ref> After "blossoming", Swampfire gains the ability to grow vines with a flame tip from his hands and use them as whips, which are able to slice the plasma generated by [[Ball Weevil]]'s [[Ball Weevil's Species|species]].<ref name="WXIP2">''[[Weapon XI: Part 2]]''</ref>

Swampfire's body structure allows him to walk straight through thin spaces such as the gaps between iron bars.<ref name="XB2" /> When he was crushed under a large container, his body deformed into vines that burrowed through and then out of the ground to reform him instantly. In the same instance, Kevin punched Swampfire in the torso, resulting in his fist getting stuck in it until Swampfire punched him back. Additionally, Swampfire is nearly impervious to physical harm{{Refn|group = AF Mini Bible|name = bible 4}} and appears to be immune to laser bolts, as they simply passed right through him and seemed to tickle him.<ref name="B10RP1" />

Swampfire is capable of regenerating and regrowing any damaged or destroyed body parts, allowing him to grow back lost limbs, holes in his body, or even his head. He was even able to regrow and reform his body from remains when it got splattered to pieces.<ref name="VoVP2">''[[Vengeance of Vilgax: Part 2]]''</ref>

Another method of regeneration involves reattaching detached or severed body parts.{{Refn|group = AF Mini Bible|name = bible 4}} This is accomplished by manipulating his vine-like "veins" and tentacles to reach out and meld with the insides of the detached limb and return them to the body, allowing him to reconstitute automatically if damaged.<ref name="B10RP1">''[[Ben 10 Returns: Part 1]]''</ref> He can also "stitch" wounds of other creatures using this method, allowing him to reattach [[Reinrassig III]]'s severed forearm.<ref name="AT">''[[Alone Together]]''</ref>

Swampfire is able to extend his fingers and feet into long roots that can dig through rock.<ref name="GT" /> Similar to [[Wildvine (Classic)|Wildvine]], Swampfire can also stretch his arms to grab objects outside his normal reach.<ref name="VoVP2" />

Swampfire has enhanced strength, being able to push over a [[Highbreed Weather Tower]] using leverage by turning his feet into roots running deep into the ground.<ref name="ETAtW">''[[Everybody Talks About the Weather]]''</ref> He was even hold his own against [[Vilgax (Classic)|Vilgax]] with his bare fists.<ref name="TFBP2" /> However, he is physically weaker than [[Crystalsapien (Classic)|Crystalsapiens]],{{Refn|[[:File:Omnitrix Transformation Duration.PNG]]|group = DM}} [[Tetramand (Classic)|Tetramands]], and [[Vaxasaurian (Classic)|Vaxasaurians]].{{Refn|[[:File:Kevin's Previous Girlfriends.PNG]]|group = DM}} Swampfire is capable of jumping exceptionally high,<ref name="ETAtW" /> as well as performing acrobatics while in the air, as seen during his fight with Negative Humungousaur.<ref name="GCBC">''[[Good Copy, Bad Copy]]''</ref>

Swampfire is immune to the lethal toxins in [[Methanos]]' atmosphere.{{Refn|''[[Ben 10 Alien Force: The Complete Guide]]''; [[:File:Methanos Landscape.png|Page 28]]|group = guide}}

Swampfire, despite being a humanoid plant, is resistant to cold temperatures.<ref name="ETAtW" />

Swampfire's body can generate a type of mud that sticks to everything but him, which he used to blind [[Albedo|Negative]] [[Humungousaur (Classic)|Humungousaur]], as the latter could not pull it off his eyes and had to change into Negative [[Big Chill (Classic)|Big Chill]] to get rid of it.<ref name="GCBC">''[[Good Copy, Bad Copy]]''</ref>

===Non-Canon Powers and Abilities===
====Cartoon Network Action Pack!====
Swampfire is being able to transform his arms into whip-like tendrils that he can use against opponents.{{Refn|[[:File:Target: Rath3.png]]|group = AP}}{{Refn|''[[Target: Rath]]''|group = AP}}

====Alien Force (Console Version)====
Swampfire can phase through the ground and "swim" underneath it at high speed, before bursting out in a coat of flames.

Swampfire can release the cloud of methane and then ignite it with a flick of his fingers, damaging nearby opponents in an explosion.

Swampfire can generate a row of thick thorns from the ground by punching it.

====Alien Force (Nintendo DS Version)====
Swampfire has ability to release fire out of his feet, allowing him to blast his opponents with flames while kicking them in the air.

====Vilgax Attacks (Console Version)====
Swampfire can ignite his fists to increase his damage output, create a ring of fire, and cause thorny vines to sprout from the ground.

====Cosmic Destruction====
Swapfire can combine his chlorokinetic and pyrokinetic abilities, making huge flaming plants sprout from the ground.

==Weaknesses==
<gallery type="slideshow">
CHS (206).png|Ineffective Fire
VoV2 (308).png|Collateral Methane Damage
WXI2 (419).png|Electricity Vulnerability
VG (146).png|Acid Vulnerability (Seed Vines)
TEC (207).png|Reptile Attraction
CaFS (243).png|Broken Arm
</gallery>
{{Quote|Lots of fertilizer down there.|Swampfire after accidentally blowing up the sewers.<ref name="VoVP2" />}}
Swampfire's fire attacks can be cancelled out by fire extinguishers<ref name="VG">''[[Video Games (Episode)|Video Games]]''</ref> and water generated by [[Orishan]].<ref name="DoN"/> His flame-based attacks in general are useless against anything that can withstand or absorb fire, such as the [[Magical Pumpkin]].<ref name="CIS" />

Unlike [[Heatblast (Classic)|Heatblast]], Swampfire cannot absorb fire to reduce the amount of collateral damage his fire causes. If he finds himself in an area filled with flammable gas, he can unintentionally cause a massive explosion.<ref name="VoVP2" />

Swampfire is ill-suited for stealth, having a strong putrid stench similar to [[Stinkfly (Classic)|Stinkfly]] and incredibly high body temperature that allows enemies to easily detect him.<ref>''[[The Eggman Cometh]]''</ref>

Swampfire can be harmed by electricity, such as that generated by a [[Conductoid]].<ref name="WXIP2" />

Swampfire's seed vines can be killed by using acid, as demonstrated by the [[Stalker]].<ref name="VG" />

If Ben turns into Swampfire with a broken limb, his limb will be twisted and shriveled, and he will feel pain from it.<ref name="CaFS">''[[Catch a Falling Star]]''</ref>

Swampfire is unable to control sapient plants, such as the [[Plant Clones]].<ref>''[[The Big Story]]''</ref>

==History==
===Alien Force===
*Swampfire first appeared in ''[[Ben 10 Returns: Part 1]]'', where he defeated some [[DNAlien]]s, [[Forever Knights]], and [[Kevin Levin (Classic)|Kevin]].
*In ''[[Everybody Talks About the Weather]]'', Swampfire battled some DNAliens, gave [[Alan Albright|Alan]] advice on flying, and destroyed the [[Highbreed Weather Tower]] with the latter's help.
*In ''[[Plumbers' Helpers (Episode)|Plumbers' Helpers]]'', Swampfire escaped the [[Null Void (Classic)|Null Void]] and defeated [[Manny Armstrong|Manny]] and [[Helen Wheels|Helen]].
*In ''[[Paradox]]'', Swampfire found and met [[Professor Paradox]] and briefly chased him around [[Los Soledad]].
*In ''[[X = Ben + 2]]'', Swampfire defeated [[SevenSeven]] and some [[Incursean (Classic)|Incurseans]] and stopped [[Attea|Princess Attea]] from destroying [[Earth (Classic)|Earth]].
*In ''[[Alone Together]]'', Swampfire defeated a large group of [[Dasypodidae]]. Later, Swampfire healed [[Reinrassig III]]'s detached hand, making his arm a partial [[Methanosian]] arm.
*In ''[[Good Copy, Bad Copy]]'', Swampfire defeated [[Albedo|Negative]] [[Humungousaur (Classic)|Humungousaur]], but was defeated himself by Negative [[Big Chill (Classic)|Big Chill]], so he switched into [[Brainstorm]].
*In ''[[Undercover]]'', Swampfire saved [[Alien Force|the team]] from an exploding [[Teleporter Pod]].
*In ''[[Grounded]]'', Swampfire was defeated by a [[Highbreed]].
*In ''[[Pet Project]]'', Swampfire fought [[Ship]], who was being controlled by [[Dr. Joseph Chadwick]] and the Forever Knights.
*In ''[[War of the Worlds: Part 1]]'', Swampfire battled an army of DNAliens before switching into [[Upchuck|Murk Upchuck]].
*In ''[[War of the Worlds: Part 2]]'', Swampfire defeated the [[Highbreed Earth Commander]].
*In ''[[Vengeance of Vilgax: Part 2]]'', Swampfire fought and recaptured the escaped [[Goop (Classic)|Goop]].
**The same scene reoccurred on TV during [[Will Harangue]]'s news report in ''[[Fame]]''.
*In ''[[Simple]]'', Swampfire captured the [[Blue Leader|Blue]] and [[Red Leader]]s and forced them to work out a peace treaty.
*In ''[[Singlehanded]]'', Swampfire, with no left hand, battled some [[Vulpimancer (Classic)|Vulpimancers]] in the Null Void. He scared them and two kids away with a fire blast.
*In ''[[If All Else Fails]]'', Swampfire took over the [[Failsafe]] in order to free [[Max Tennyson (Classic)|Max]].
*In ''[[Trade-Off!]]'', Swampfire was defeated and almost had his powers drained by [[Michael Morningstar (Classic)|Darkstar]], but was saved and got his powers back due to Kevin's intervention.
**The same scene reoccurred in a flashback in ''[[Absolute Power: Part 1]]''.
*In ''[[Ghost Town]]'', Swampfire protected a young [[Chimera Sui Generis (Classic)|Chimera Sui Generis]] girl from some [[Ectonurite (Classic)|Ectonurites]].
*In ''[[Busy Box]]'', Swampfire fought the [[Vreedle Brothers]].
*In ''[[The Final Battle: Part 1]]'', [[Albedo|Negative]] Swampfire defeated and captured Gwen.
*In ''[[The Final Battle: Part 2]]'', Swampfire was used by Vilgax's [[Bioid]]s to try and kill Ben and his team before the [[Omnitrix (Original)|Omnitrix]] self-destructed, thus reverting them. Later, Ben as Swampfire fought [[Vilgax (Classic)|Vilgax]] before using the [[Ultimatrix (Original)|Ultimatrix]] to go [[Ultimate Swampfire|Ultimate]].

===Ultimate Alien===
*In ''[[Fame]]'', Swampfire made a cameo on TV.
*In ''[[Hit 'Em Where They Live]]'', Swampfire battled [[Zombozo (Classic)|Zombozo]], [[Vulkanus]], and [[Charmcaster (Classic)|Charmcaster]].
*In ''[[Video Games (Episode)|Video Games]]'', Swampfire was scanned by [[Oliver Thompson]] for the [[Stalker]] off-screen. Later, he failed to defeat the Stalker, so he switched into [[Jetray (Classic)|Jetray]].
*In ''[[Andreas' Fault]]'', Swampfire saved [[Andreas]] from [[Sir Dagonet]] and the [[Forever Knights]].
*In ''[[Ultimate Aggregor (Episode)|Ultimate Aggregor]]'', Swampfire went [[Ultimate Swampfire|Ultimate]] to fight the [[Aggrebot]]s that were patrolling [[Los Soledad]].
*In ''[[Perplexahedron (Episode)|Perplexahedron]]'', Swampfire thawed [[Gwen Tennyson (Classic)|Gwen]] out of some ice.
*In ''[[The Forge of Creation]]'', Swampfire went Ultimate to battle [[Ultimate Aggregor]].
*In ''[[Eye of the Beholder]]'', Swampfire went Ultimate to fight the [[Sentinels of Monawk]]. Swampfire appeared again later when he was changing back to [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]].
*In ''[[The Big Story]]'', Swampfire fought the [[Plant Alien]] but failed to defeat it before going Ultimate. Swampfire appeared again later when he was changing back to Ben.
*In ''[[Ben 10,000 Returns]]'', Swampfire went Ultimate to fight [[Eon]] only to be destroyed by the latter's time ray. After Eon was defeated, however, Swampfire was restored by [[Ben 10,000 (Ultimate Alien)|Ben 10,000]].
*In ''[[The Creature From Beyond]]'', Swampfire disarmed two Forever Knights and [[Sir Cyrus]] before battling the [[Lucubra]].
*In ''[[Basic Training]]'', Swampfire destroyed a shooting target in the [[Plumbers' Academy]].
*In ''[[Prisoner Number 775 is Missing]]'', Swampfire lit a campfire.
*In ''[[Simian Says]]'', Swampfire battled some [[Arachnachimp (Classic)|Arachnachimp]] [[DNAlien]]s and cured DNAlien [[Eunice]].
*In ''[[Catch a Falling Star]]'', Swampfire, with a broken arm, broke into the dog pound with Gwen.
*In ''[[The Eggman Cometh]]'', Swampfire was defeated by some [[Pterodactyl|pterodactyls]].
*In ''[[Night of the Living Nightmare]]'', Swampfire defeated Albedo, who was disguised as Gwen, before switching into [[Fasttrack]] in a dream.

===Omniverse===
*In ''[[Have I Got a Deal for You]]'', Swampfire failed to stop the [[Screegit]].
*In ''[[Return to Forever]]'', Swampfire tried to break out of a force field, but was reverted by the [[Forever Knights]]' DNA scanner.
*In ''[[Charmed, I'm Sure]]'', Swampfire was used four times. Firstly, he appeared when [[Charmcaster (Classic)|Charmcaster]] teleported to [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]]. The other three times, Swampfire battled [[Magical Pumpkin]], [[Anur-Mirrored Ben]], and Charmcaster in her [[Alpha Rune]] Armor, all while he was slowly maturing into his blossomed form.
**Also, [[Anur-Mirrored Ben|Anur-Mirrored]] Swampfire was destroyed by the real Swampfire.
*In ''[[Weapon XI: Part 2]]'', Swampfire was defeated by [[Weapon XI (Present)|Mutant Kevin]].
*In ''[[A New Dawn]]'', Swampfire appeared for a short time when Ben was cycling through his aliens.

===[[Time Heals Timeline]]===
*In ''[[Time Heals]]'', Swampfire battled [[Charmcaster (Classic)|Charmcaster]] and her [[Rock Monster]]s and defeated [[Hex (Classic)|Hex]].

