==Trivia==
*Swampfire is the reason why [[Kevin Levin (Classic)|Kevin]] has an x-shaped scar on his chin.<ref name="WXIP2" />
**Interestingly, Swampfire's first and last appearance (not counting cameos) are him fighting Kevin. However, this is just a coincidence.{{Refn|[[:File:Swampfire vs Kevin fight is a coincidence.png]]|group = CM}}
*Swampfire is one of the four regular aliens to get a complete redesign in '''[[Ben 10: Omniverse (TV Series)|Omniverse]]'''; the others being [[Shocksquatch]], [[Eatle]], and [[Chromastone (Classic)|Chromastone]]. However, Swampfire and Chromastone are the only two of these aliens to get redesigns mid-series (not counting [[Rath (Classic)|Rath]] getting clothes).
*Swampfire and [[Big Chill (Classic)|Big Chill]] are the only aliens whose natural biological behavior has overridden [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]]'s normal state.
**Methanosians undergo a kind of growth and "blossoming" phase. In Ben's case, his [[Omnitrix (Omniverse)|Omnitrix]] was unable to select a different alien and he kept developing large facial pustules in his human form until Swampfire had fully blossomed.<ref name="CIS" />
*Swampfire is the first alien used in '''[[Ben 10: Alien Force (TV Series)|Alien Force]]'''. The first alien used in the '''[[Ben 10 (2005 TV Series)|Original Series]]''' ([[Heatblast (Classic)|Heatblast]]) also has fire-based powers like Swampfire.
**Swampfire is also the first alien that Ben used via the [[Ultimatrix (Original)|Ultimatrix]].
**Ironically, Swampfire was the last transformation used by [[Vilgax (Classic)|Vilgax's]] [[Bioid]]s via the original Omnitrix.
*Despite not having a nose, Swampfire somehow has a sense of smell.<ref name="B10RP1" /><ref name="CaFS" />
*Swampfire is one of the four regular aliens to be temporarily destroyed and removed from the [[Omnitrix (Original)|Omnitrix]]/Ultimatrix; the others being [[Way Big (Classic)|Way Big]], Chromastone, and [[Feedback]].
*[[Blitzwolfer]] and Swampfire are the only known aliens to have temporary transition forms.
*Swampfire's appearance in ''[[Video Games (Episode)|Video Games]]'' was the first mistransformation in '''[[Ben 10: Ultimate Alien (TV Series)|Ultimate Alien]]'''.
*During the pre-production of '''Alien Force''', Swampfire was conceived as a mixture between [[Wildvine (Classic)|Wildvine]] and [[Heatblast (Classic)|Heatblast]].{{Refn|http://archive.is/cLKJJ|group = GM}}
**In ''[[The Forge of Creation]]'', 10-year-old [[Stinkfly (Classic)|Stinkfly]] describes Swampfire, as well Ultimate Swampfire, as "a copy of Wildvine."
**Swampfire's '''Alien Force''' design went through heavy revisions, with concept art drawn by [[Glenn Wong]], [[Eric Canete]],{{Refn|[[:File:Eric Canete Designed Swampfire Concepts.png]]|group = EC}} [[Thomas N. Perkins IV]],{{Refn|http://archive.vn/CBTLC|group = TNP}} and [[Glen Murakami]]. The final design was created by Glen Murakami, with color styling by Chris Hooten.{{Refn|[[:File:Swampfire preproduction details.PNG]]|group = GW}}
*Swampfire was originally supposed to appear in:
**''[[Inside Man]]'' to save [[Tyler]] from a police officer disguised as a [[DNAlien]].{{Refn|[https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ben10/images/2/24/Inside_Man_Script_Outline.pdf/revision/latest ''Inside Man'' Script Outline]|group = outline}}
**''[[Moonstruck]]'' to light a campfire.{{Refn|[https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ben10/images/f/ff/Moonstruck_Script_Outline.pdf ''Moonstruck'' Script Outline]|group = outline|name = outline}}
*Swampfire's blossoming was [[Derrick J. Wyatt]]'s idea, as he wanted to use some of Thomas Perkins' unused Swampfire concept art.{{Refn|[[:File:DJW Thought Of Swampfire Blossoming.PNG]]|group = DJW|name = redesign}} The final design was created by [[Steven Choi]].{{Refn|[[:File:Steven Choi Designed Blossomed Swampfire.png]]|group = SC}}
**Derrick stated that the design was difficult to finalize. He didn't like anything and the crew kept going around and around because he didn't know what he wanted. Initially, he preferred Swampfire's redesign over his '''Alien Force''' design, but he was "still kind of there" to him.{{Refn|[[:File:Swampfire's Blossomed Design Was Difficult.png]]|group = DJW}} Years later, when asked which design he preferred, he replied with "Eh".{{Refn|[[:File:Derrick's Preferred Swampfire Design.png]]|group = DJW}}
*Had Negative Swampfire appeared in '''Omniverse''', he would have looked like the unblossomed version of the transformation.{{Refn|''link unavailable''|group = DJW|name = link unavailable}}
*Derrick preferred [[Ultimate Swampfire]] to Swampfire, calling him a million times better.{{Refn|[[:File:Derrick's Opinion on the Ultimates' Designs.png]]|group = DJW}}

